Z||000000||BroCar 87||09-03-2000||04:28 AM||||Hey fella's, I am inquiring on the 4 cylinder performance rebuild kit that The Fiero Store sells. It comes with <BR>Hyperutectic Pistons<BR>Sealed Power Cam Kit<BR>Sealed Power Rings<BR>Felpro Gaskets<BR>Freeze Plug Kit<BR>Timing Gear Set<BR>Federal Mogul Bearings<BR>Standard Oil Pump<P>All this for $490.00. Has anyone ever done this or know what kinda gains I can get from doing this? I have a 1987 coupe that has 110,000 miles. I have only had it since April, so I don't know how tired it is. KNOWING it comes with a performance cam package, I BELIEVE IT WOULD BE BETTER.<BR>Thanks for any info!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLFieroSIG.jpg">  <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||6
Z||000001||StuGood||09-03-2000||02:02 PM||||I suspect this isn't the answer you really wanted to hear, but why don't you just do a compression check before you spend that kind of money on parts (and downtime)?  That way, you'll have an idea "how tired it is."  <P>After that, give it a <B>thorough</B> tune-up.  It costs very little, and then you'll have a good feel for what the baseline performance of the engine is like, before you do any mods.  $490 sounds like a lot of money, if all you really get out of it is a camshaft and gasket kit.       ||||reg||4
